  (a) Making profit.
  (b) Accurately representing Extropianism.

The problem with commercialization is that it assigns primary importance to
what the market wants to hear, not to what you want to say.  I would prefer
that we say what's important to us, whether it makes us any money or not.
=46or this reason, I am, in general, opposed to the commercialization of
Extropianism.

